Package: remlax
Type: Package
Title: Generic, Differentiable REML Solver for Linear Mixed Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Nicolas", family = "Salas",
                  email = "nicolas.salas@supagro.fr",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits linear mixed models by restricted maximum likelihood
    (REML; Patterson and Thompson (1971) <doi:10.1093/biomet/58.3.545>) with a
    formula grammar close to that of 'ASReml-R'. The likelihood is formed on the
    dense marginal covariance matrix and differentiated automatically by a
    solver written with 'JAX', which runs unchanged on CPU or GPU. The R side
    builds and checks the design, writes it to a temporary directory as raw
    binary files with a 'JSON' manifest, calls the 'Python' solver as a
    subprocess and reads the result back. Covariance structures follow the
    'ASReml-R' catalogue (idv, idh, corgh, fa, rr, chol, ante, corh; ar1, ar2,
    ar3, ma, arma, corb, corg, exp, gau, sph, cir, Matern, separable products).
    Helpers build weighted neighbourhood incidences for direct and indirect
    genetic effects in mixtures of two species, as in the model of Salas et al.
    (2026) <doi:10.64898/2026.05.27.728303>. A second, sparse engine built on
    'RTMB' covers the structures whose precision matrix is sparse and known in
    closed form. The 'Python' solver ships with the package; a 'Python'
    (>= 3.10) interpreter with 'jax', 'numpy' and 'scipy' must be available,
    and rx_install_python() creates one on request. The validation against
    'asreml', 'lme4', 'sommer' and 'nlme' is shipped as a vignette, and
    rx_validate() reruns the comparisons against the packages available on
    CRAN.
License: GPL (>= 3)
